WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.468 line:0%
-Chloe, you do
so many great impressions,

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.870 line:0%
and I wanted to challenge you
to something fun.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.339 line:0%
We all want to
get in the holiday spirit,

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.007 line:0%
so here's what we're gonna do.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.410 line:0%
I'd love you to start
reading the classic poem

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.912 line:0%
"'Twas the Night
Before Christmas," okay?

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.582
And as you're reading, there
will be names of celebrities

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.516
that pop up onscreen, okay?

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:20.453
So you'll keep reading
but in the voice of
whoever comes up next.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.089
And you could wear that scarf
if you'd like to.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.424
You don't have to.
-Ooh! Well, it does
match my outfit.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.060
-It actually really does.
-Yeah. Holiday vibes!

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.462
-Okay, here we go. Ready?

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.364
Whenever you're ready,
you can start

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.433
with the first impression
that appears on the screen

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.435
right over there.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.236
Roots, can we get
some sleigh bells?

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:38.570
[ Sleigh bells jingling ]

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.073 line:0%
-[As Reese Witherspoon]
Ahem.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:41.474 line:0%
Okay, 'twas the night
before Christmas,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.476 line:0%
when all through the house,
not a creature was stirrin',

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.711 line:0%
not even a fierce
little mouse, y'all!

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.613 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] Okay.
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:48.982 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ] Okay.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.983 line:0%
[As Drew Barrymore]
The children were nestled

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:54.420 line:0%
all snug in their amazing beds,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.424 line:0%
while visions of
the most gorgeous sugarplums

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:01.360 line:0%
danced in their head.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.929 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.198 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ] Oh!
Okay, this one.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.667 line:0%
-Margaret Thatcher.
-You got the teeth -- the teeth.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.969 line:0%
[As Margaret Thatcher]
When out on the lawn,

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:13.573 line:0%
there arose
an unfavorable clatter,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:17.577 line:0%
I sprang from my bedchambers

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.114 line:0%
to see what was the matter.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.149 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God!
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.184 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ] Oh, good.

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.553 line:0%
I have to pretend this is
a shawl for Nicole Kidman.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.155 line:0%
-All right.
-Okay.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.590 line:0%
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.593 line:0%
[As Nicole Kidman] Away to the
window I jumped like a 'roo,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.897 line:0%
tore open the shutters,
and [laughs]

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:41.134 line:0%
Oh, my God, what a view.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.002 line:0%
-Oh, my God.
[ Bell dings ]

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.904 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ] Oh.
All right, here we go.

00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:48.240 line:0%
[As Phoebe Waller-Bridge]
'Twas a little old chap

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.842 line:0%
so cheeky and quick,

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.379 line:0%
I knew in a moment
he must be Saint Nick.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.415 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]
-[ Bell dings ]

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.486 line:0%
-[As Timothée Chalamet]
Uh, he -- he had a broad face

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.356 line:0%
and a, uh, little round belly

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.925 line:0%
that shook when he laughed
like a bowl of jelly.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:08.528 line:0%
[ Laughs ]
Nah, nah, nah.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:11.664 line:0%
I'm sorry, Nick.
Nah, nah, nah.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.266 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.568 line:0%
-[ Normal voice ]
Ah, okay. This one's fun.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.171 line:0%
Ah, well, you know,
to get into Meryl Streep,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.174 line:0%
I kind of have to adjust my hair
a little bit.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.009 line:0%
[As Meryl Streep]
Ah, well, you know...

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:26.713 line:0%
But I heard him exclaim,
as he drove out of sight,

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:31.584 line:0%
Meryl Christmas to all
and to all a good night!

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.120 line:0%
-Chloe Fineman, everybody!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.921 line:0%
That is how you do it
right there!

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.189 line:0%
I thought I'd do
something with you

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.391 line:0%
because you're always fun

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.192 line:0%
and we have fun
every time you come on here.

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:42.061 line:0%
But you do a lot of great
different accents,

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.495 line:0%
and I wanted to challenge you
to something fun.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.264 line:0%
So here's what I'd like you
to do here.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.432
This is a book right here.
It's a beautiful book.

00:02:47.432 --> 00:02:49.101
-A leather-bound book.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:50.637
-Yes, this is from
my home collection.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.104
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.039
This is the classic poem "'Twas
the Night Before Christmas."

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.541
-Oh, okay.

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.109
-And what I thought you could
do is maybe, as you're reading,

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.311
a different accent will come up
on the screen there.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:00.780
-Okay.
-And when the bell rings,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.749
you change and read the book
in that accent.

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.150
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.951
Could you do that, maybe?
-I'll give it a go, yeah.

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:10.122
-Yeah. I also have a nice,
festive scarf

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:11.524
I can place upon you.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:15.461
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.096
Yeah. And then --

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.564
-Ten points for Gryffindor!

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.633
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.835
-Yeah. All right.
All right. There you go.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.637
So, that's it.
It's all nice and festive.

00:03:25.637 --> 00:03:26.839
-[ Clears throat ]
-Now here we go.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.174
[ Both clear throat ]
You can start reading

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.677
with the first accent
that appears on the screen.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.411 line:0%
Roots, can we get some
sleigh bells maybe?

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:33.679 line:0%
-♪♪
-Scot--

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.114 line:0%
-Aww.
-Scottish.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.850 line:0%
-Aw. That's cute.
Scottish. Okay.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.219 line:0%
-[Scottish accent] 'Twas
the night before Christmas,

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:44.390 line:0%
when all through the house,
not a creature was stirring,

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.159 line:0%
not even a wee, little 'moose.'"

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.661 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell dings ]

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.895 line:0%
-A moose.

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.196 line:0%
-[Russian accent]
"Stockings were hung

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:53.333 line:0%
by the chimney with care,

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.369 line:0%
in hopes that Saint Nicholas
soon arrive."

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:59.639 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.106 line:0%
-Spanish.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.808 line:0%
-[Spanish accent] "The children
were very, very happy."

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.277 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:09.682 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.951 line:0%
-Oh, my God.
-Oh, oh, Please, please.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.553 line:0%
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.654 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
-This is my turn, okay?

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.290 line:0%
-Oh, yeah, sorry, sorry.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.125 line:0%
-"The children
were very, very happy,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.494 line:0%
all snug in their beds,

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:25.565 line:0%
while visions of sugarplums
danced in their cabeza."

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:26.732 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell dings ]

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.167 line:0%
-Cabeza?

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.668 line:0%
-[Rural American accent]
"And Mom in her kerchief

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:32.839 line:0%
and I in my cap...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:36.309 line:0%
had just kicked back
for a little catnap."

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.010 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell dings ]

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.313 line:0%
Whoo!
[ Cheering and laughter ]

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:43.182 line:0%
-[French accent]
"When out of the roof,

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.718 line:0%
there arose such a clatter.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:51.423 line:0%
I sprang from my bed to see --
how you say, uh...

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:53.292 line:0%
what was the matter."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.593 line:0%
[ Bell dings ]

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:56.461 line:0%
"It was frickin' Santa Claus!"

00:04:56.461 --> 00:04:59.098 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.799 line:0%
-Oh, my God.

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:05.071 line:0%
-"It was Santa Claus,
with his little round belly

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:08.207 line:0%
that jiggled when he walked
and talked

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.476 line:0%
like a bowl full of spaghetti."

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.077 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell dings ]

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.979 line:0%
-[Australian accent]
"And I heard him exclaim

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.249 line:0%
as he drove out of sight,

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:19.085 line:0%
Merry Christmas to all
and g'day, mate."

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:22.621 line:0%
-Oh, my gosh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:24.957 line:0%
Wow!

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.558 line:0%
One of my favorite parts
of the holidays

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:28.660 line:0%
is reading "'Twas the Night
Before Christmas."

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.729 line:0%
But I don't have time
to read the whole thing

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:32.030 line:0%
right here, right now,

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.632 line:0%
but fortunately
I know someone who can.

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:36.969 line:0%
Ladies and gentlemen,
a shortened, more casual version

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.471 line:0%
of "'Twas the Night
Before Christmas"

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.706 line:0%
is Nick Offerman,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:40.706 --> 00:05:43.743 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.111 line:0%
[ Indistinct conversation ]

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:47.513 line:0%
Nick Offerman.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.181 line:0%
Thank you so much.
I appreciate this.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.983 line:0%
Nick Offerman.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:54.554 line:0%
Nick, whenever you're ready,
take it away.

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.689 line:0%
-All right.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:01.193 line:0%
It was Christmas Eve,
and the house was really quiet.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:05.163 line:0%
You couldn't even hear rodents,
like mice, crawling around.

00:06:05.163 --> 00:06:08.500 line:0%
Some kids were sleeping
and dreaming of sugar plums

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.203 line:0%
and other random [bleep].

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:14.406 line:0%
And then a fat bearded man
broke into their house

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.743 line:0%
and put toys into a sock.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.646 line:0%
Then he climbed in a sleigh
and flew off,

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.915 line:0%
like the down of a thistle,

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:25.451 line:0%
whatever the [bleep] that means.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.786 line:0%
The end.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:28.721 line:0%
-Thank you very much.
Nick Offerman, everyone.

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:31.758 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.991 --> 00:06:35.761 line:0%
'Twas the night
before Christmas,

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.763 line:0%
when all through the house

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:41.066 line:0%
not a creature was stirring,
not even a mouse.

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:43.335
-I hate that mouse.

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:45.504
Always hear him walking around
with his little nails

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:48.040
scratching against
my kitchen floor.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.544
I got brand-new floors, Jim,
from France.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.780
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:59.952
-The stockings were hung
by the chimney with care,

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:03.055
In hopes that Saint Nicholas
soon would be there.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.690
-When's that dude gonna show up?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.792
I've been waiting up
all night for him.

00:07:06.792 --> 00:07:09.095
Santa Claus is late!

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:16.135
-The children were nestled
all snug in their beds

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:19.605
while visions of sugar plums
danced in their heads.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.309
-Sugar plums?
You definitely don't got kids.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.043
I got three kids.

00:07:25.043 --> 00:07:29.214
They want a WiiU, Xbox,
a ColecoVision, "Call of Duty."

00:07:29.214 --> 00:07:31.918
Not one of them asking me
for no sugar plum.

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:34.220
By the way, I know a pimp
named Sugar Plum.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:43.328
When out on the lawn
there arose such a clatter,

00:07:43.328 --> 00:07:46.365
I sprang from the bed
to see what was the matter.

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:48.634
-It was a Tempur-Pedic bed, too.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:50.202
You know the ones
in the commercial

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:52.538
where they drop a bowling ball
on the bed...

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:55.074
but the wine glass
never spills over?

00:07:55.074 --> 00:07:57.276
Which is good because my
favorite thing to do in a bed

00:07:57.276 --> 00:08:00.179
is bowling
and drinking red wine.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:09.555
-When what to my wondering eyes
should appear

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:12.791
but a miniature sleigh
and eight tiny reindeer.

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:14.693
-Eight tiny reindeer?
Ha ha ha ha!

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.529
That's hilarious!

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.002
-With a little old driver
so lively and quick,

00:08:24.002 --> 00:08:26.171
I knew in a moment
he must be Saint Nick.

00:08:26.171 --> 00:08:29.141
"Now, Dasher! Now, Dancer!
Now, Prancer and Vixen!

00:08:29.141 --> 00:08:32.344
On, Comet! On, Cupid!
On, Donner and Blitzen!"

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:34.046
-I like to call them
by their nicknames.

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:36.014
Scooter, Porkchop,
Captain Freak,

00:08:36.014 --> 00:08:39.151
DJ Downing McFresh,
Bonzai, Mr. Dimples,

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.220
Spanky, and Joe Frazier.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.369
-As I drew in my head
and was turning around

00:08:57.369 --> 00:09:00.372
down the chimney Saint Nicholas
came with a bound.

00:09:00.372 --> 00:09:03.542
-Chimneys are like
brickhouse penises.

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:05.278
That's a poem I wrote.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:08.681
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.619 --> 00:09:16.956
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:21.526 --> 00:09:24.363
-He had a broad face
and a little round belly

00:09:24.363 --> 00:09:27.967
that shook when he laughed,
like a bowl full of jelly.

00:09:27.967 --> 00:09:29.835
-But I don't know
what he's laughing about.

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:33.172
There's nothing funny
about obesity.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:35.174
Unless you're those two fat
motorcycle guys

00:09:35.174 --> 00:09:37.108
from the Guinness Book
of World Records.

00:09:37.108 --> 00:09:40.546
Those guys are funny.
Can we see a picture of them?

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:44.517
[ Laughing hysterically ]
Thanks, Dave!

00:09:48.654 --> 00:09:52.191
-He sprung to his sleigh,
to his team gave a whistle.

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:55.027
And away they all flew
like the down of a thistle.

00:09:55.027 --> 00:09:58.664
But I heard him exclaim,
ere he drove out of sight...

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:01.934
-Happy Christmas to all,
and to all a good night.

00:10:01.934 --> 00:10:04.070
[ Cheers and applause ]

